hem safer so that  design makes a huge difference and that  attitude has been missing from a lot of  american safety so are we likely to  suddenly see roads across the u.s become  narrower and filled with trees and  curbside shops anytime soon well  according to beth if the biden  administration wants to slow down  america's roads to potentially save  lives it's gonna have to do so quickly  you've got to slowly rehab our entire  massive national transportation system  which isn't going to happen overnight  but mass infrastructure change can be a  huge expensive task and while some  streets may change in the short term  it's unclear what the longer term  effects of this plan could be or how  many lives it could save it's still a 10  to 20 year process  and you know if they lose this window  that 10 to 20 years again if there's a  change of leadership or something shifts  can turn into 40 years like that so in  the interim it's going to be up to the  drivers themselves to try and reduce the  number of accidents so drive safe folks  hey thanks for watching so do you think  the speed limit on america's road should  be reassessed let me know in the  comments below and as always if you're  interested in the future of how we might  be getting from a to b then don't forget  to subscribe see you soon  [Music]
 

